<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Audiencia</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as audiencias</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">An audiencia was a high court of justice in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spanish-empire">Spanish Empire</a>, which in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/americas">Americas</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/philippines">Philippines</a> also exercised administrative and political functions. Its judges, called oidores, heard appeals and advised or checked the viceroys and governors. The audiencias were a key part of the crown's system of colonial governance.</p></div>
